## exp026: Model Soup — ❌ 失败

**Method**: Arithmetic weight averaging of AmpPredictor checkpoints (Wortsman et al. 2022 "Model Soups"). No training required.

### Results

| Variant | Amp Corr | Amp RMSE(log) | f0 RPA |
|---------|----------|---------------|--------|
| exp023 (source 1) | **0.676** | 0.726 | 95.56% |
| exp024 (source 2) | 0.668 | **0.695** | 95.30% |
| exp025 (source 3) | 0.665 | 0.731 | 95.09% |
| **2-way soup** (exp023+024) | **0.601** ❌ | **2.761** ❌ | 95.56% |
| **3-way soup** (exp023+024+025) | **0.586** ❌ | **3.746** ❌ | 95.32% |

### Key Findings

- **Catastrophic failure**: Amp Corr dropped from 0.676→0.601 (-11%), RMSE exploded from 0.726→2.761 (+280%)
- **Root cause**: Weight spaces are incompatible — different training configs (dropout 0.3 vs 0.4, MSE vs CorrLoss, weak vs strong regularization) place weights in different loss basins. Averaging crosses high-loss barriers
- **3-way soup worse than 2-way**, confirming basin incompatibility
- f0 metrics unchanged (same diffusion model)

